  "title": "How Did Bankrupt Marvel Become a $4B Deal?",
  "tag": "Company backstory",
  "description": "Marvel went bankrupt. So why did Disney still pay 4 billion?\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Marvel Entertainment: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvel_Entertainment\n- Wikipedia: Marvel Studios: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvel_Studios\n- Wikipedia: Iron Man (2008 film): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_Man_(2008_film)\n- Wikipedia: Marvel Cinematic Universe: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvel_Cinematic_Universe\n\nFrom the cited Wikipedia pages: December 27 1996, the Marvel group of companies filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy; June 2 1998, Toy Biz and Marvel Entertainment Group merged into Marvel Enterprises to bring it out of bankruptcy; September 2005, Marvel announced a $525 million Merrill Lynch financing deal backed by the film rights to ten characters, to make its own films; Iron Man (2008) grossed $585.8 million worldwide; December 31 2009, Disney completed its purchase of Marvel Entertainment for about $4 billion. Photos: Wikimedia Commons (credits below). Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #marvel #movies #howtheymakemoney",
